{
  "manifestVersion": 1,
  "id": "player",
  "category": "player",
  "status": "provisional",
  "comment": "THE PROTAGONIST, from the user's own pose sheet (art/player/source/hero-sheet.png) — made by `npm run assets:animate` from art/player/source/hero.poses.json (which drawing is which), hero.rig.json (where the parts of each drawing are) and tools/assets/heroClips.ts (how they move): 114 frames in 18 clips, every pixel of every frame a pixel of the user's drawings, moved and never drawn, recoloured or smoothed (a rigid, smooth warp bends the body, the head, the antennae, the legs; the blade of the sword is a rigid piece that turns about its hilt). 9 clips are STAND-INS (tag \"stand-in\"): the motion is real but the sheet has no drawing of their action, so the drawing of another one is what moves — crouch: the sheet has no crouch: the drawing of the landing crouch is held, breathing; crouchWalk: the sheet has no crouched walk: the drawing of the landing crouch shuffles along; dash: the sheet's dash drawing is a red streak, not a figure: the dive drawing of the run is thrown forward instead; attack2: the sheet's second blow cannot be separated from its red arc: the drawing of the first blow is swung the other way; aerialAttack: the sheet has no blow in the air: the drawing of the first blow is moved to fit one (legs drawn up); crouchAttack: the sheet has no blow from the crouch: the drawing of the first blow is lowered onto its legs; death: the sheet has no death: the drawing of the hit is turned onto the floor; drink: the sheet has no drinking: the standing drawing does the gesture (there is no drawing of a bottle; the potion's light is the effect's); interact: the sheet has no interaction: the standing drawing leans in and nods (no hand reaching is made up). `npm run assets:missing` counts them as NOT delivered. Hand over drawn frames for a clip and the stand-in goes away.",
  "tags": [
    "protagonist"
  ],
